{"2362620": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "LEGION:DEAD METAL", "steam_appid": 2362620, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In a world where history has been quietly shaped from the shadows, two factions have waged a hidden war for centuries.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The Legion operates in silence—an elite, deniable force tasked with containing threats the world was never meant to see. Their mission is simple: identify the danger, isolate it, and erase it before it spreads.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Opposing them are the Fallen.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Not a nation. Not an army. Something far more dangerous.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Their influence can be traced through humanity’s darkest moments—most notably during World War II, where they embedded themselves within global power structures, manipulating events to accelerate destruction and instability. They do not seek recognition. Only control.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Now, a covert military research facility located in international waters has gone silent.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Forty-eight hours ago, all communication ceased.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Official reports cite a systems failure—but long-range scans tell a different story. The facility is still drawing power. Controlled. Intentional.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Someone is still there.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Intelligence suggests the Fallen have taken control.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The facility itself is highly classified, housing advanced robotics programs, experimental bio-research, and next-generation mechanized combat platforms—technology capable of shifting the balance of power if it falls into the wrong hands.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If the Fallen secure it, they won’t just disappear into the shadows.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >They’ll escalate.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Elijah Stone is deployed alone.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A Legion operative trained for high-risk infiltration and containment, Stone is inserted with a single objective: assess the situation, locate the source of the takeover, and neutralize any threat before it can leave the island.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >No backup. No extraction guarantee.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >What begins as a standard recon mission quickly deteriorates into a full-scale incursion. The facility is no longer under military control. Patrols have changed. Systems have been repurposed. And whatever the Fallen are building… it’s already in motion.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Cut off from support and deep behind enemy lines, Stone must fight through a compound that is rapidly transforming into something else—something weaponized.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Because this was never just about taking the facility.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >It was about what the Fallen could turn it into.</p>", "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In a world where history has been quietly shaped from the shadows, two factions have waged a hidden war for centuries.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The Legion operates in silence—an elite, deniable force tasked with containing threats the world was never meant to see. Their mission is simple: identify the danger, isolate it, and erase it before it spreads.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Opposing them are the Fallen.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Not a nation. Not an army. Something far more dangerous.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Their influence can be traced through humanity’s darkest moments—most notably during World War II, where they embedded themselves within global power structures, manipulating events to accelerate destruction and instability. They do not seek recognition. Only control.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Now, a covert military research facility located in international waters has gone silent.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Forty-eight hours ago, all communicati